<article class="env-definition" id="040H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/040H">Definition <span data-tag="040H">29.25.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>submersive</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000640472" id="a0000640472-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if the continuous map of underlying topological spaces is submersive, see Topology, Definition <a href="/tag/0406" data-tag="0406">5.6.3</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is <em>universally submersive</em> if for every morphism of schemes $Y' \to Y$ the base change $Y' \times _ Y X \to Y'$ is submersive. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>